      "description": "**Question.** Can the subject hold a cued location in memory over a delay and then look there? (The paper used this trial to find prefrontal delay activity in monkeys; this set is the behaviour only, for a human volunteer.)\n\n**What is on the screen.** A small white fixation spot. After [[param:fixation_period]] of held fixation, a white square cue flashes for [[param:cue_duration]] at one of eight locations [[param:cue_ecc_dva]] out, 45° apart. Then nothing but the spot for the delay (1.5, 3 or 6 s, [[param:delays]]). The spot going off is the go signal.\n\n**What the subject does.** Looks at the spot within [[param:acquire_timeout]] and keeps gaze inside the fixation window through the cue and the delay (eye tracker; leaving it ends the trial and it is served again), then saccades to the remembered cue location within [[param:response_period]].\n\n**Varied.** Cue location (8) and delay (3), shuffled within each block.\n\n**Measured.** Saccade landing: inside the [[param:target_window_dva]]-radius window around the cue is CORRECT, elsewhere INACCURATE (kept); latency and landing error per location and delay.\n\n**What it can and cannot show.** Memory-guided saccade accuracy for this subject. It cannot show the paper's result, the directional delay-period firing of single prefrontal neurons, which needs a recording. A video tracker counts a blink as a fixation break, so a human must not blink for up to 7.25 s; calibrate before the session.",
      "sourceFiles": [
        "src/funahashi1989/task.py",
        "src/funahashi1989/stimuli.py",
        "configs/task.yaml",
        "configs/task-monkey.yaml",
        "configs/rig-booth.yaml"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Paper values: 0.1° white spot, 0.7° white square cue, 13° eccentricity, eight locations, 0.75 s fixation, 0.5 s cue, 1.5/3/6 s delays, 0.5 s response period, 6° response window, 5 s inter-trial interval (pp. 331–333).",
        "ASSUMED (not in the paper): the 1.5 dva fixation window radius, the 2 s limit to acquire fixation, the landing rule (first sample slower than 30 dva/s, at most 150 ms) and the trial counts.",
        "Deviation: mid-grey field instead of the dark screen; the human set is instructed and unpaid.",
        "configs/task-monkey.yaml is the same trial for the paper's subject, adding juice for a correct saccade; only its last block differs.",
        "Human set (configs/task.yaml): instructed, unpaid, fixation enforced by the eye tracker. Monkey set (configs/task-monkey.yaml): same trial plus juice on CORRECT; reward volume must be measured on the rig."
      ]
